<?php declare(strict_types=1);require_once __DIR__.'/includes/ui.php';pv_page_start('Privacy','',pv_is_logged_in());?><main class="nxt-document"><section class="pv-card pv-prose nxt-document-panel"><div class="nxt-document-head"><div><span class="pv-eyebrow">DIGIMON NXT / NETWORK INFORMATION</span><h1>Privacy</h1></div><?=nxt_sprite('keramon')?></div><p>Accounts store usernames, password hashes, email addresses, login metadata and gameplay state in the configured local MariaDB/MySQL database. Password plaintext is never stored. Server operators control and are responsible for the database they host.</p><p>The server records request times, IP addresses, account names, page paths, response status and selected gameplay actions for local administration. Its World Server journal excludes passwords, cookies, request bodies, private message contents and URL query values, and rotates as it grows. Administrative changes have a separate database audit. The hosting web server may also maintain access logs under the operator's own configuration.</p></section></main><?php pv_page_end();?>
